.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt I2C-DEV 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm i2c-dev
.Nd run I2C and SMBus transfers on an I2C bus
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /dev/i2c-N
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Each I2C adapter has a character device, major 89 and minor
.Ar N ,
its number, through which root runs transfers on the bus, as Linux's
i2c-dev gives them.
The adapters are the display's buses of
.Xr i915 4 :
each GMBUS pin's, named as Linux names them, such as
.Ql i915 gmbus dpb ,
and each eDP and DisplayPort channel's I2C over AUX, such as
.Ql AUX A/DDI A/PHY A .
The kernel numbers them from 0 in that order, the lowest number free, and
creates each node as root:root with mode 0600.
A transfer wakes the device if it sleeps, and runs under the device's mode
lock.
.Pp
A
.Xr read 2
or
.Xr write 2
of up to 8192 bytes is one message to or from the address
.Dv I2C_SLAVE
set.
The requests of
.In linux/i2c-dev.h :
.Bl -tag -width I2C_SLAVE_FORCE
.It Dv I2C_SLAVE , I2C_SLAVE_FORCE
Set the address of reads, writes and
.Dv I2C_SMBUS ,
at most 0x7f, or 0x3ff with
.Dv I2C_TENBIT .
No kernel driver holds an address here, so the two are the same.
.It Dv I2C_TENBIT
Take addresses as ten bits when the argument is not 0.
Neither bus sends them, and their transfers fail.
.It Dv I2C_PEC
Append and check the SMBus packet error code of each
.Dv I2C_SMBUS
transfer but the quick and I2C block ones when the argument is not 0.
.It Dv I2C_FUNCS
Store the adapter's
.Dv I2C_FUNC_
bits in the
.Vt unsigned long
at the argument:
.Dv I2C_FUNC_I2C
and
.Dv I2C_FUNC_SMBUS_EMUL .
.It Dv I2C_RDWR
Run the
.Vt struct i2c_rdwr_ioctl_data
at the argument, up to 42 messages of up to 8192 bytes each, as one
transaction with a repeated start between them.
The answer is the number of messages run.
.It Dv I2C_SMBUS
Run the
.Vt struct i2c_smbus_ioctl_data
at the argument, made of I2C messages as Linux's emulation makes them:
quick, byte, byte data, word data, process call, block write, and I2C
block read and write.
.It Dv I2C_RETRIES
Try a transfer the adapter answers
.Er EAGAIN
this many times more.
.It Dv I2C_TIMEOUT
Stop those tries after this many tens of milliseconds; 1 second by
default.
.El
.Pp
An i386 program on the x86-64 kernel makes the same requests with its own
structures, which the kernel translates.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:02.0/i2c-N
.It Pa /sys/devices/.../drm/cardN/cardN-CONNECTOR/i2c-N
An adapter's directory, below the PCI function for a GMBUS pin and below
its connector for a DisplayPort channel, with
.Pa name ,
.Pa uevent
and a
.Pa subsystem
link to
.Pa /sys/bus/i2c .
.It Pa .../i2c-N/i2c-dev/i2c-N
The node's directory, with
.Pa dev ,
.Pa name ,
.Pa uevent ,
.Pa device
and a
.Pa subsystem
link to
.Pa /sys/class/i2c-dev .
.It Pa /sys/bus/i2c/devices/i2c-N
.It Pa /sys/class/i2c-dev/i2c-N
.It Pa /sys/dev/char/89:N
Links to those directories, through which udev finds the device.
.It Pa /sys/devices/.../drm/cardN/cardN-CONNECTOR/ddc
A link to the adapter that reads the connector's EDID: an eDP or
DisplayPort connector's channel, an HDMI connector's GMBUS pin.
.It Pa /sys/module/i2c_dev/initstate
.Ql live ,
as a loaded
.Pa i2c-dev.ko
reads, so that
.Ql modprobe i2c-dev
succeeds, once an adapter is added.
.El
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er ENODEV
The adapter's device was unbound.
.It Bq Er ENXIO , EREMOTEIO
No device answered the address on a GMBUS pin or a DisplayPort channel.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
An address out of range, a ten-bit address, more than 42 messages, a
message over 8192 bytes, an SMBus block over 32 bytes, or an unknown SMBus
size or direction.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
A message with
.Dv I2C_M_RECV_LEN ,
or an SMBus block read or block process call, whose length the device
sends first, which neither bus reads.
.It Bq Er EBADMSG
The packet error code does not match.
.It Bq Er EFAULT
A structure or buffer cannot be read or written.
.It Bq Er ENOTTY
The request is unknown.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ioctl 2 ,
.Xr read 2 ,
.Xr write 2 ,
.Xr i915 4
